    "body": "Hello @ggerganov I did local benchmarks with this PR and here are my results:\r\n\r\nRTX 4070 Laptop GPU, CUDA, Q4_K_M models, `llama-bench -ngl 99 -p 512 -n 128 -r 5`, with `-t` as the thread count below. Values are tokens per second.\r\n\r\n| model | threads | test | b11399 | master | PR 30160 |\r\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\r\n| Qwen3-VL-2B | 8 | tg128 | 183.9 | 166.2 | 182.5 |\r\n| Qwen3-VL-2B | 32 | tg128 | 183.8 | 153.9 | 182.4 |\r\n| Qwen3-VL-2B | 8 | pp512 | 11912 | 10210 | 11571 |\r\n| Qwen3-VL-2B | 32 | pp512 | 12474 | 10517 | 11372 |\r\n| Gemma 4 E2B | 8 | tg128 | 131.4 | 122.3 | 121.7 |\r\n| Gemma 4 E2B | 32 | tg128 | 130.8 | 114.9 | 115.1 |\r\n| Gemma 4 E2B | 8 | pp512 | 7618 | 8057 | 7842 |\r\n| Gemma 4 E2B | 32 | pp512 | 7699 | 7731 | 8078 |\r\n\r\nmaster is c811cb8f0, the base of PR 30160 at 4e67ebbe4. b11399 is the release before PR 29622. pp512 varies about 3 percent from run to run.\r\n\r\nSo in short it does handle the performance slowdown thank you!\r\n\r\nOf course, as already noted in the current TODO Gemma 4 still suffers from a performance hit, but perhaps that if for another PR?",
