    "body": "Here are my benchmarks, however it appears that Gemma4 with embeddibng only batches now crashes.\r\n\r\nFirst the numbers:\r\n\r\nRTX 4070 Laptop GPU, CUDA, Q4_K_M models, `llama-bench -ngl 99 -p 512 -n 128 -r 5`, with `-t` as the thread count below. Values are tokens per second.\r\n\r\n| model | threads | test | b11399 | master | PR 30160 |\r\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\r\n| Qwen3-VL-2B | 8 | tg128 | 183.8 | 166.7 | 182.5 |\r\n| Qwen3-VL-2B | 32 | tg128 | 183.8 | 154.4 | 182.4 |\r\n| Qwen3-VL-2B | 8 | pp512 | 12454 | 10402 | 12079 |\r\n| Qwen3-VL-2B | 32 | pp512 | 12463 | 10574 | 11958 |\r\n| Gemma 4 E2B | 8 | tg128 | 131.4 | 123.3 | 130.9 |\r\n| Gemma 4 E2B | 32 | tg128 | 131.4 | 115.9 | 130.9 |\r\n| Gemma 4 E2B | 8 | pp512 | 7714 | 8153 | 8081 |\r\n| Gemma 4 E2B | 32 | pp512 | 7545 | 8199 | 8099 |\r\n\r\nMy coding tools gave this reason for the crash:\r\n  - With 1 row: ggml-cpu/ops.cpp:4987: fatal error, because ggml_scale gets the Q5_K tensor without the cast to F32.\r\n  - With 8 rows: ggml.c:3758: GGML_ASSERT(ggml_nelements(a) == ne0*ne1*ne2), because one padding row is reshaped to n_tokens rows.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
